"Correct is C: it refuses the binary while fully answering the underlying question (what is our risk, where is it going, what remains, what would it cost to reduce) \u2014 the decision-useful brief boards actually want. A is wrong: 'yes' is a hostage to the next incident. B is wrong: 'no' without the risk detail is abdication dressed as philosophy. D is wrong: declining pushes the work back; the professional contributes the analysis.",
